# EN: reads the faired border network (work/retopo/network.npz) and the clean shell (work/retopo/shell.npz) and writes, in lines/data/ :
#       lines.json     : nodes, arcs as clamped uniform cubic B-splines (control points only, see ZrlSpline.py), mirror arc ids, components
#       view_<n>.png   : shaded orthographic render of the shell (grey Lambert, light pastel tint per component, white background)
#       depth_<n>.png  : the same view as a 16 bit depth map (0 = empty, else depth = depth_offset + value / 65535 * depth_scale)
#       views.json     : per view the camera (center, px_per_m, res, rx, uy, tz) and the depth encoding
#       export_report.json : fit errors, mirror quality, arc ends that are off their node (read it before trusting the junctions)
#     Pixel convention (same as Raster.py) : col = (p - center).rx * s + res/2 - 0.5 ; row = res/2 - 0.5 - (p - center).uy * s.
#     python ZrlExport.py            everything      |   python ZrlExport.py --skip-views   only lines.json (seconds, no GPU)
# FR : exporte le réseau de lignes en B-splines éditables, les vues orthographiques ombrées, leurs cartes de profondeur et un rapport.
